{"name":"Cheerful Heart","hex":"#dcc7c0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cheerful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Noticeably happy and optimistic.","Bright and pleasant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheerful"},{"term":"heart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A muscular organ that pumps blood through the body, traditionally thought to be the seat of emotion.","One's feelings and emotions, especially considered as part of one's character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be fond of. Often bracketed or abbreviated with a heart symbol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To mark a comment, post, reply, etc., with the heart symbol (❤)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Happiness","blocks":[{"text":"Happiness is a complex and multifaceted mental state that encompasses a range of positive feelings, from contentment to intense joy. It is often associated with positive life experiences, such as achieving goals, spending time with loved ones, or engaging in enjoyable activities. However, happiness can also arise spontaneously, without any apparent external cause."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Girl_of_Vietnam.jpg/330px-Girl_of_Vietnam.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Happiness"},{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Sweet_Baby_Kisses_Family_Love.jpg/500px-Sweet_Baby_Kisses_Family_Love.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Sweet_Baby_Kisses_Family_Love.jpg/1280px-Sweet_Baby_Kisses_Family_Love.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Sweet_Baby_Kisses_Family_Love.jpg/500px-Sweet_Baby_Kisses_Family_Love.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Woman kissing a baby on the cheek","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASweet_Baby_Kisses_Family_Love.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/My_Grandfather_Photo_from_January_17.JPG/500px-My_Grandfather_Photo_from_January_17.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/My_Grandfather_Photo_from_January_17.JPG/1280px-My_Grandfather_Photo_from_January_17.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/My_Grandfather_Photo_from_January_17.JPG/500px-My_Grandfather_Photo_from_January_17.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 93-year-old man from Pichilemu, Chile","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMy_Grandfather_Photo_from_January_17.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/US_Navy_110527-N-OA833-014_Newly_commissioned_Navy_and_Marine_Corps_officers_toss_their_hats_during_the_U.S._Naval_Academy_Class_of_2011_graduatio